Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-09-2000||01:29 AM||||I want to put a standard in my automatic 87GT...  How difficult of a conversion is it??   I tried the search funtion,but, it won't work tonight for me...   I think trying to do all the cables and linkage would be the worst part.... has anyone here done the conversion???  thank's    Steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-09-2000||09:31 AM||||Things off hand:<BR>Brake and clutch pedals.<BR>Master, line and slave.<BR>Shifter and cables (new shifter plate).<BR>Clutch kit, flywheel and drive shafts.<BR>Tranmission w/mounts (a given).<BR>Prom chip for computer.<BR>I always miss something!<BR>Sounds like more work than it is!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-10-2000||02:04 PM||||I believe the engine wiring harness between the C-500 connector and the engine is slightly different.  At least the ones on my 85se V-6 4spd and my 85 GT auto are.<P>The auto has wiring for the shift selector.  The speed sensors are different (at least in different locations but the plug might work on both).  And the wiring to the rear hatch release is different between auto and std.<P>It may not be a big deal to adapt, I haven't put much thought into it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-10-2000||04:00 PM||||TCC output from the ECM now needs to go to the Upshift indicator on the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MooCow||10-10-2000||06:23 PM||||Is it easer to switch from a 4-speed stick to an auto??  I just hate driving the Fiero because it is a stick.  I don't mind driving my ranger and it is a stick so is it really hard to do??<P>                               Thanks Ken||||reg||5
